So when choosing a planet to visit your first stop should be the Tracking Station's Knowledge Base. Here you can learn more about each CB and see if you're up to the task, but for today there's no need because I know where we're going: Duna.SocialRewardSocket is already connectedSocket not supportedSoft Mask/SoftMask doesn't support image type {0}. Image type Simple will be used.SoftMask doesn't support sprites with an alpha split textureSoftMask doesn't support tight packed spritesSoftMask may not work because its defaultShader is not setSoftMask will not work on {0} because material {1} doesn't support masking. Add masking support to your material or set Graphic's material to None to use a default one.SoftenSolar Insolation At Home: Solar Luminosity At Home: Solar Panel EfficiencySolar flux in W/m^2 at the orbital altitude of the homeworldSolarEjectionMultiplierSolarOrbitHeatToleranceSolidFuelSomeSome <b>test</b> values
Get <i>Displayed Here</i>
in <color=orange>multiple lines</color>
and rich-text formattedSome VPWheelCollider references are missing at the Axles property.
All axles should have a reference to the corresponding left-right VPWheelCollider objects.Some kOS settings are now tracked seperately per-game using the stock settings menu. 

You currently seem to have some of these settings stored in kOS's global folder, probably because you were using a previous version of kOS in the past. You can migrate these settings from their global (now unused) location into this game's individual settings if you like. (Note that the telnet server settings are still kept globally, but everything else has moved.)

<color=#ffffff>The new place to adjust the settings in-game is in the <color=#ffff00>"Difficulty Options"</color> button of the in-game settings window. (Press <color=#ffff00>ESC</color>, pick <color=#ffff00>Settings</color>, then <color=#ffff00>Difficulty Options</color>, then <color=#ffff00>kOS</color> to reach them now.)
The settings are there despite them not really being about "Difficulty". That's just the location where KSP allows mods to make custom parameters.</color>

